CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cast to a same-width pointer type: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
reinterpret_cast<long *> of a `long long *' kept the source type, since
irept comparison ignores #c_type and conditional_cast left the operand
alone.  Overload resolution then selected the wrong function or none: with
the MSVC STL, `__iso_volatile_load32(reinterpret_cast<volatile int *>(&x))'
for a `long' x (_Incref_nz in <memory>, 26 failures on VS 2022).
